  "definitions": {
    "fail_closed": "Selector refuses current selection because authority changed or an enumeration requiring completeness was interrupted.",
    "false_omission_branches": "Missing branches while the strategy nevertheless proceeds as if discovery were complete.",
    "mutable_hotspot_write_attempts": "Synthetic shared mutable index-root write/CAS attempts; immutable checkpoint/manifest creation is excluded.",
    "undiscoverable_branches": "Existing immutable branches missing from the strategy's discovered set, regardless of whether the selector fails closed."
  },
  "findings": [
    "A mutable shared branch-index root can preserve all branches only by retrying same-base CAS conflicts; at 32 branches the modeled retry slice averages 62 shared-root write attempts and 32 recovery reads, while an orphaned index write remains invisible.",
    "Pinned-tree checkpoint-path enumeration had zero false omissions and zero shared mutable hotspot writes in the finite model; incomplete/interrupted enumeration fails closed rather than claiming completeness.",
    "Sharded immutable manifests and pending receipts remove the mutable index hotspot but still falsely omit a checkpoint when that checkpoint exists and its manifest/receipt was never durably created.",
    "A parent-linked DAG reachable only from current LATEST cannot discover concurrent sibling branches; every modeled scenario with n>1 had undiscoverable branches.",
    "Duplicate manifest/receipt paths must dedupe by checkpoint identity, not manifest identity, and current authority must be revalidated after discovery."
  ],
